<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02QQ">Exercise <span data-tag="02QQ">9.7.2.11</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{\leq 1}$ denote the full subcategory of $\operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}$ spanned by the objects $[0]$ and $[1]$, which we depict informally as a diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ [0] \ar@ &lt;.8ex&gt;[r] \ar@ &lt;-.8ex&gt;[r] &amp;  [1]. \ar [l] } \]
</div>
<p> Show that: </p>
<p><ul>
<li><p>
The opposite category $\operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{\leq 1}^{\operatorname{op}}$ satisfies condition $(\ast )$ of Warning <a data-tag="02QF" href="/tag/02QF">9.7.2.2</a> (that is, it is a sifted category in the sense of <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/MR1815045">MR1815045</a>]</span>). 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The simplicial set $\operatorname{N}_{\bullet }( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}_{\leq 1}^{\operatorname{op}})$ is not sifted. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>
